Bugfix: Save calendar events with an attendee address mail cannot go to

Saving an event over CalDAV whose ATTENDEE carries an address without a
domain - `MAILTO:hausmeister`, or `MAILTO:undefined` as the calendar app writes
for an attendee added with an empty field - failed the whole PUT with HTTP 500.
The event was not stored, and the invitations to the valid attendees were not
sent either. This hit every CalDAV client, not only the calendar app.

Two things went wrong. OC\Mail\Message split every address at the '@' and fed
the missing domain to idn_to_ascii(), which under PHP 8 throws a ValueError on
an empty string - an Error that none of the callers' `catch (\Exception)`
blocks sees. And the iMIP plugin of the dav app built the invitation outside
its try block, so any exception from the mail layer aborted the request.

An address without a usable domain part is now handed on unchanged, and the
mail layer rejects it with its regular exception. The iMIP plugin sets the
recipient first and catches that rejection: for an address no mail can go to
it leaves out just that invitation, marks the attendee with SCHEDULE-STATUS 3.7
(invalid calendar user), logs a warning naming the address and saves the
event. The check is exactly the one the mail layer applies when sending, so
every address that got an invitation before still gets one - including a
domain with an underscore or a blank before or after the address, which a
first version of this fix left out. A sender address the mail layer rejects
now also ends in SCHEDULE-STATUS 5.0 instead of an aborted save.
